[{:db/id "answer-field-b1439bbb-bd02-5648-b8fa-4994eaa3e108" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1439bbb-bd02-5648-b8fa-4994eaa3e108" :answer-field/correct "answer-2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba" :answer-field/choices [17592186649974 17592186649973 17592186649972 17592186649975 17592186649976 "answer-2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba"] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba" :answer/id #uuid "2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=-41i+31j-23k" :answer/feedback "Locally authored correction by Codex; this option was absent from the original Math Academy bank." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186649977 :question/worked-solution "Local correction by Codex. The five original Math Academy choices are retained; the additional correct equation is locally authored. Math Academy's grading key for the original bank is unconfirmed.\n\nWe need a vector parallel to the line. Using the two given points,\n\n$$\nv=q-p=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\8\\\\9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\-1\\\\4\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\\\9\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nStarting with $(r-p)\\times v=0$, we obtain $r\\times v=p\\times v$. Expanding the cross product gives\n\n$$\np\\times v=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\-3&-1&4\\\\4&9&5\\end{vmatrix}\n=(-5-36)i-( -15-16)j+(-27+4)k=-41i+31j-23k.\n$$\n\nThus the equation is\n\n$$\nr\\times\\begin{bmatrix}4\\\\9\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}=-41i+31j-23k.\n$$\n\nBoth given points satisfy this equation: $P\\times v=Q\\times v=(-41,31,-23)$. None of the five original choices does.\n\nOriginal Math Academy explanation (preserved verbatim below; its concluding signs are incorrect):\n\nWe know that the line passes through the points $P(-3,-1,4)$ and $Q(1,8,9).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, starting with the equation of the line using the cross product, we manipulate the equation and then substitute in our values of $p$ and $v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v-p\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v & =p\\times v \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =-41i-31j+23k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1439bbb-bd02-5648-b8fa-4994eaa3e108"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
